    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d643">

                <pb facs="0731" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg417"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/311</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in. Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-12-24">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">December 24, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 2:45 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Berlin’s 1171, 22d. Am informed further half-month dyestuff supply has been
                    released amounting to about 1,100 tons for shipment on <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Berwind</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
